!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-record-written-in-place-may-not-state-a-chain-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2"
  description: """
    A type written in place carries no `chain`: it has no name, so it is IS-A nothing and nothing composes it. The
    record `at` holds in place states `base` as a supertype, a resolver error at `order` stating that rule. A
    processor that refuses it only where its own model is built, with that model's message, has the verdict and
    not the rule.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
